            <ArticleTitle>A large necrotic defect secondary to a cutaneous sinus tract of odontogenic origin: a case report.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>362, 364, 366 PASSIM; QUIZ 372</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This article reviews the case of a patient with a periapical dental abscess that drained inferior and posterior to the angle of the jaw and created a large purulent cutaneous defect. Both the diagnosis and treatment issues are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
